---
import MaterialPage from "@/components/MaterialPage.astro";
import { materialBySlug } from "@/data/materials";

const entry = materialBySlug("flies");
if (!entry) throw new Error("Unknown material");
---

<MaterialPage entry={entry}>
  <p slot="intro">
    <code>FliesMaterial</code> redraws your text as a swarm. Each point lives in its own small cell
    on the text and wanders around it, tirelessly, occasionally trespassing on a neighbour. From a
    distance the word holds together; up close it never sits still. Turn on dodging and the swarm
    parts around a position you feed it, which is how the pointer example in the guide works.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="uPointCellWidth">
    <p>Imagine a grid laid over the text. Each point moves mostly within one cell of it, and this is the cell’s width and height.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uPointCellWidth-value">
    <p>A float from <code>0.0</code> to <code>1.0</code>, as a fraction of the text’s total height. On a 100-pixel-tall text, <code>0.04</code> gives 4-pixel cells.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uPointRadius">
    <p>The size of each point.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uPointRadius-value">
    <p>A float from <code>0.0</code> to <code>1.0</code>, relative to half a cell. At <code>1.0</code> a point fills its cell edge to edge.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uDodge">
    <p>A switch. When on, points shrink away from <code>uDodgePosition</code> across the distance set by <code>uDodgeSpread</code>. The usual use is a pointer sweeping through the word.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uDodge-value">
    <p>A float used as a boolean: <code>0.0</code> for off, <code>1.0</code> for on.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uDodgePosition">
    <p>The position the swarm avoids while <code>uDodge</code> is on.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uDodgePosition-value">
    <p>A pair of floats from <code>0.0</code> to <code>1.0</code>, relative to the text’s width and height. The origin is the bottom-left corner, as in WebGL, so a pointer position from the DOM needs its <code>y</code> flipped: <code>[x, 1 - y]</code>.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uDodgeSpread">
    <p>How far from <code>uDodgePosition</code> the shrinking reaches.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uDodgeSpread-value">
    <p>A float from <code>0.0</code> to <code>1.0</code>, as a fraction of the text’s total height.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uSpeed">
    <p>How fast the points move.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uSpeed-value">
    <p>Any float. It multiplies <code>uGlobalTime</code>, the seconds since the effect started, so <code>0.0</code> freezes the swarm and <code>2.0</code> doubles its pace.</p>
  </Fragment>
</MaterialPage>
